      "text": [
        " سَمِعْتُ أَبِي سَأَلَ أَبَا عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) وَ أَنَا أَسْمَعُ فَقَالَ لَهُ رُبَّمَا أَمَرْنَا الرَّجُلَ فَيَشْتَرِي لَنَا الْأَرْضَ وَ الدَّارَ وَ الْغُلَامَ وَ الْجَارِيَةَ وَ نَجْعَلُ لَهُ جُعْلًا قَالَ لَا بَأْسَ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "A number of our companions, from Sahl Bin Ziyad, and Ahmad Bin Muhammad, from Ibn Mahboub, from Abdullah Bin Sinan who said, ",
          "‘I heard my father asking Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> and I was listening, so he said to him<sup>asws</sup>, ‘Sometimes we instruct the man so he buys for us the land, and the house, and the slave, and the slave girl, and we make a fee to be for him’. He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘There is no problem’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "4. A number of our people have narrated from Sahl ibn Ziyad and Ahmad ibn Muhammad from ibn Mahbub from ‘Abd Allah ibn Sinan who has said the following: “Once, a man asked abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, when I was listening, ‘We perhaps order a man to buy for us land, house, slave or slave-girl and assign for him a certain amount. He (the Imam) said, ‘It is not unlawful.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
